15... Rxf3 $1 { A natural and strong decision. At the cost of an exchange, Black destroys White's pawn structure. The main targets are the f-pawns and the d4-pawn. } ( { Another option was } 15... e5 $5 16. Nxe5 Nxe5 17. dxe5 Qxe5 { and the resulting structure will be studied in the next example. } ) 
 ( 15... Be8 { would be well met by } 16. Ng3 { preventing the annoying ...Bh5. } ) 
16. gxf3 e5 $1 { Planning ...Bh3 to turn the bad bishop into a dangerous weapon. Black's position is not necessarily superior yet, but White's defence is very hard to conduct due to the multiple threats. } ( { After the imprecise } 16... Qg5 17. Kh1 Qh5 18. Ng3 Qh4 19. Ne2 { Black only gets a draw by repetition after } Qh5 ( { But } 19... e5 $5 { is also a worthy alternative. } ) 
 ( { While } 19... Nxd4 $4 { loses to } 20. Nxd4 Qxd4 21. Bxh7 ) 
 ) 

